  "synopsis": "Frankie Doyle, 49, played Inspector Ray Cole on 'Cole Justice' for nine seasons and has played nothing since. Teaching an acting masterclass in a Bristol community hall, he performs his legendary interrogation scene — Cole confessing to throw the real killer off — the same night a property developer is murdered two streets away, in circumstances matching, detail for detail, a 'Cole Justice' episode Frankie wrote. His class's phones hold forty minutes of Frankie performing motive, method and remorse. The detective assigned grew up watching the show, which helps, then really doesn't. With his ex-wife — his former co-star, now a true-crime podcaster monetizing his arrest — and his class turned amateur legal team, Frankie must solve the crime with the only expertise he has: thinking like a fictional detective, and like his murderers. One of whom, he realizes, is in his class, taking notes.",
